  "question": {
    "text": "The radius of the second Bohr orbit for hydrogen atom is<br /><br />(Planck&#39;s constant, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>.6262</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>34</mn></mrow></msup><mi>Js</mi><mo>;</mo></math>&nbsp;mass of electron <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>.1091</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>31</mn></mrow></msup><mi>kg</mi><mo>;</mo></math> charge of electron <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.60210</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>19</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>;</mo></math>&nbsp;permittivity of vacuum, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8712;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.854185</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi>kg</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>)",
